course: dictionary
lesson: 10442
title: One word, many meanings: true
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word true can mean different things. Read the words around it to find the right meaning. «The first paragraph tells who, what, when and where.» Here, true means right and real, agreeing with the facts, not made up.
explain: «A true friend» is a friend who stays loyal to you. «My wish came true» means it really happened. «The shelf is not true» means it is not straight. Same word, three different jobs.
explain: People also say «so true» when they agree with someone. That is casual talk. Before you agree, check the facts. Ask yourself: is it really true?
fact: True means right and real, agreeing with the facts, not false or made up.
fact: «A true friend» means a loyal friend who stays with you.
fact: «My wish came true» means it really happened.
fact: True can also mean straight or exact: «the shelf is not true» means it is not straight.
fact: «So true» is casual talk meaning you very much agree, so check the facts first.
exercise: «Nine-year-old Ella Brown rescued six ducklings from a drain on Monday.» In a report like this, what should true mean? | Straight and exact | *Real, agreeing with what actually happened | Made up and invented | Loyal and faithful
exercise: «My wish came true.» What does this mean? | It broke in half | It was a lovely wish | *It really happened
exercise: A friend says «So true!» What does this casual phrase mean? | *I agree very much | It is raining | I am lost
test: In «the shelf is not true», what does true mean? | Made up | Real and right | Loyal | *Straight and exact
test: Before you agree with a friend who says «so true», what should you do first? | Shout yes straight away | Ask for a snack | *Check whether the facts agree | Change the subject
exam: Which statement is true? | Two plus two makes five | Two plus two makes nine | Two plus two makes six | *Two plus two makes four
